WEBVTT

00:03:58.836 --> 00:04:00.036
"Why are you praying?

00:04:00.076 --> 00:04:02.236
You never got an answer back, did you?

00:04:02.236 --> 00:04:03.836
So why are you praying?"

00:04:03.876 --> 00:04:05.276
And the man thinks about it

00:04:05.316 --> 00:04:08.676
and is troubled
by the cynic's observation.

00:04:08.716 --> 00:04:14.356
And he falls into a fitful sleep during
which he's visited by Khidr,

00:04:14.396 --> 00:04:17.436
the guide of souls, who says to him,

00:04:17.476 --> 00:04:18.836
"Why did you stop praying?"

00:04:18.876 --> 00:04:21.316
And he said, "Well, you know,
God never answered me,

00:04:21.356 --> 00:04:22.516
Allah never answered."

00:04:22.556 --> 00:04:25.796
And this is what Khidr
says to him, he says,

00:04:25.836 --> 00:04:28.596
and now I'm quoting from the poem itself,

00:04:28.636 --> 00:04:32.396
"This longing you express
is the return message.